Map every logical stack in one SET_LOGICAL_SLOT_MAPPING.

`slot-map` sends a single mapping, and the array index *is* the logical stack
id on the wire, so it can only ever address stack 0. On a dual-SIM s5400 that
makes it destructive: pointing it at the eUICC evicts whatever was on stack 0,
taking voice and SMS down with it.

`slot-maps` takes one SLOT[:PORT] per stack, in stack order, so both can be
placed in a single request -- `slot-maps 2:0 1:0` keeps the physical card on
stack 0 and puts the eUICC on stack 1, which is where the CP pins it whenever
both are mapped. Without this the eUICC stays unmapped, and sit-lpa reports
"no mapped, active eUICC port" so lpac cannot reach it at all.

